This repository contains the Flash-Next engine overlay ("build-6"), an overlay on
vLLM, the open-source LLM inference and serving engine.

  vLLM
  https://github.com/vllm-project/vllm
  Copyright contributors to the vLLM project
  Licensed under the Apache License, Version 2.0

Base version the overlay applies to:
  vLLM commit   dc36fcce902a63eab06c1b93a5c4a5ee178a0c56
  vLLM version  0.29.1rc1.dev47+gdc36fcce9
  Docker image  vllm/vllm-openai:nightly-dc36fcce902a63eab06c1b93a5c4a5ee178a0c56
                (image id sha256:ad067db5d64ed30b52f5aa9ae88d7645e71ff1842c876d7db116fed617a5cd0b)

The files below are copies of vLLM source files from that commit, modified by
us. Each one carries a "[crazydiamond-on-ampere] MODIFIED vLLM FILE" header
under its original SPDX lines. At run time the launcher mounts these files over
the upstream paths inside the unmodified vLLM image (vision/model.py is mounted
only in configurations without the e3/ directory, so build-6 does not use it).

  Published path (under packet/harness/native30_overlay/)   Upstream path
  core/block_pool.py                                         vllm/v1/core/block_pool.py
  core/single_type_kv_cache_manager.py                       vllm/v1/core/single_type_kv_cache_manager.py
  core/scheduler.py                                          vllm/v1/core/sched/scheduler.py
  model_runner_v2.py                                         vllm/v1/worker/gpu/model_runner.py
  e2_sources/scheduler_output.py                             vllm/v1/core/sched/output.py
  e2_sources/block_table.py                                  vllm/v1/worker/gpu/block_table.py
  e3_sources/executor.py                                     vllm/v1/executor/multiproc_executor.py
  e3_sources/core.py                                         vllm/v1/engine/core.py
  e3_sources/worker.py                                       vllm/v1/worker/gpu_worker.py
  e3_sources/cudagraph_utils.py                              vllm/v1/worker/gpu/cudagraph_utils.py
  e3_sources/sampler.py                                      vllm/v1/worker/gpu/sample/sampler.py
  e3_sources/async_utils.py                                  vllm/v1/worker/gpu/async_utils.py
  e3_sources/api_routers.py                                  vllm/entrypoints/launchers/api_server/routers.py
  e3_sources/model.py                                        vllm/models/qwen4_exp/nvidia/model.py
  ops_qsa_indexer.py                                         vllm/models/qwen4_exp/nvidia/ops/qsa_indexer.py
  e3_sources/mm_budget.py                                    vllm/multimodal/encoder_budget.py
  e3_sources/mm_encoder.py                                   vllm/v1/worker/gpu/mm/encoder_runner.py
  e3_sources/anthropic_serving.py                            vllm/entrypoints/anthropic/serving.py
  qsa.py                                                     vllm/models/qwen4_exp/nvidia/qsa.py
  ops_qsa.py                                                 vllm/models/qwen4_exp/nvidia/ops/qsa.py
  vision/model.py                                            vllm/models/qwen4_exp/nvidia/model.py

All other source files are original work of the crazydiamond-on-ampere
contributors, licensed under the Apache License, Version 2.0. Some of them call
vLLM, PyTorch, Hugging Face transformers and NVIDIA CUDA/CUPTI APIs that ship
inside the vLLM image; none of that code is copied into this repository.

Not included: the vLLM image, model weights, and compiled binaries. The model
used is Intel/Qwen3.8-Flash-Next-W4A16-AutoRound; it is referenced by name only
and is subject to its own license.
